        <!-- ============ caption ============ -->
        <mxCell id="cap" value="Fig. 1. Overall architecture of GAST. (a) The gap-aware evidence encoder converts the incomplete history into actor encodings H: an observation-evidence state (eligibility, age, reliability ρ_t = exp(−τ·Δ_t), learnable τ) drives the GERE spatial stage (per-frame agent attention conditioned on relational geometry) and the ECTA temporal stage (reliability-modulated causal Mamba ×4 with evidence-weighted state aggregation). (b) The gap-aware goal decoder builds an anchor state from the last observation and gap features, refines 20 mode queries via cross-attention, predicts gap-shifted endpoints, and decodes each mode as a linear anchor-to-endpoint path plus a decaying residual with Laplace scales and mode scores. A five-term loss (regression, classification, Laplace, endpoint, diversity) supervises training; a neighbor head predicts other agents for scene interaction." style="text;html=1;fontSize=10;fontStyle=0;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontColor=#202124;fontFamily=Times New Roman;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="742" width="1060" height="40" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

